    "done_when": "First the census corrections: its optional-subsystem roots gain the FAIR-MAST acquisition modules that import the data extra's members, and opencv (cv2), torchvision, imageio, imageio-ffmpeg and lpips are listed by name as lazily imported members of a new video extra. Both tests/test_declared_dependencies.py and tests/physics/test_dependency_contract.py resolve an editable install's checkout through one shared helper in tests/distribution_sources.py that applies unquote to the file URL path. Then pyproject.toml: every distribution the census classes default and imas_ambix/ imports goes in [project.dependencies]; tests-only imports and the tooling (pytest, pytest-cov, pytest-timeout, pytest-xdist, ruff, mypy, pre-commit, tokamap) go in [dependency-groups] dev, and the dev extra is removed; distributions imported only by the training stack (hydra-core, wandb, accelerate) sit in the train extra, uvicorn in the agent extra, and chronos-forecasting in the dependencies because core code imports it; no new [tool.uv.sources] entry; [tool.pytest.ini_options] gains timeout = 300; no version bound is added. uv.lock is regenerated with UV_OFFLINE=0 command uv lock and never uv sync, and 'UV_OFFLINE=0 command uv lock --check' exits 0. The census test's xfail marker is removed and 'UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/.venv PYTHONPATH=$PWD command uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_declared_dependencies.py tests/physics/test_dependency_contract.py' passes. 'UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/.venv PYTHONPATH=$PWD command uv run --no-sync pytest --collect-only -q -p no:cacheprovider' run before and after the edit, each logged, reports the same test count and zero errors. 'UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/.venv PYTHONPATH=$PWD command uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests' exits 0.",
